    {
      "text": "man should not counsel fellow man, D&C 1:19. those who set at naught counsels of God will incur his vengeance, D&C 3:4. thou hast suffered counsel of thy director to be trampled, D&C 3:15. receive misery if thou slight these counsels, D&C 19:33. seek not to counsel your God, D&C 22:4. you are not pardoned, because you seek to counsel in your own ways, D&C 56:14. listen to counsel of him who has ordained you, D&C 78:2 (103:5). Saints who were cast out of inheritance esteemed lightly the Lord’s counsel, D&C 101:8. people should hearken to the Lord’s counsel, D&C 103:5. if chosen follow counsel, they shall receive power, D&C 105:37. receive counsel of him whom I have appointed, D&C 108:1 (124:89). virtuous shall seek counsel, D&C 122:2. his reward shall not fail if he receive counsel, D&C 124:16. those who seek not the Lord’s counsel shall have no power, D&C 136:19.",
